{
  "id": "28244_hagureru",
  "headword": "はぐれる",
  "reading": "はぐれる",
  "romaji": "hagureru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb-ichidan",
  "gloss": "to get separated from; to lose sight of (one's group)",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to get separated from; to lose sight of (one's companions)",
      "explanation": "To become separated from a group or companion one was with, typically by accident in a crowd or while moving. The person or animal one loses is marked with と or から."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "28244_hagureru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{子供|こども}が{親|おや}とはぐれた。",
      "english": "The child got separated from its parents.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28244_hagureru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{人混|ひとご}みで{友達|ともだち}とはぐれてしまった。",
      "english": "I lost sight of my friend in the crowd.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28244_hagureru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{登山中|とざんちゅう}にグループからはぐれて、{一人|ひとり}で{下山|げざん}した。",
      "english": "I got separated from the group while climbing and came down the mountain alone.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Usually written in kana. Often appears in the resultative はぐれている (have become separated, am lost).\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Intransitive ({自動詞|じどうし}); has no transitive pair.\n- Pattern: AがBと/からはぐれる (A gets separated from B)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {親|おや}とはぐれる: get separated from one's parents\n- {群|む}れからはぐれる: stray from the herd/flock\n- はぐれた{子犬|こいぬ}: a stray puppy that lost its owner",
